WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Does squaring a sum mean just squaring each individual term?

2
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Let us test x = 1 to check if both sides give the same value.

3
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Picture a large square with total side length (a + b).

4
00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:01.000
The total area combines the two squares and two rectangle terms!

5
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Now expand (x + 3)^2 correctly by including the 2ab term.

6
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:31.500
Checking x = 1 gives 1 + 6 + 9 = 16. It works!
